@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Advisory brief: usage-aware routing ("usage profiles") in Agent Config Studio
+
+## THE ASK
+Cris (sole dev of ACS, a local web app + CLI for configuring Claude Code / Codex / Grok setups) hits usage limits on one subscription (e.g. Claude) and wants an easy way to move work (orchestrator, builders, reviewers, security, advisor) onto another account (e.g. Codex: Sol/Astra) WITHOUT editing his default roles, then switch back. He wants it flexible ("whatever I want it to be"). He believes this is a common problem for other users with other account mixes (one Claude plan only; Claude + Codex; several Claude/Codex seats; API keys), and wants the product shape right for them, not just for him.
+
+## WHAT WE KNOW
+- Roles live in ~/.agent-config-studio/roles.json (keys: version, flavor, roles{builder, reviewer, investigator, advisor, judge, security, writer, researcher}); each role = ordered families (first is the answer, rest fallbacks), effort, optional second opinion. Code: /Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/agent-config-studio-trunk/lib/roles.js, defaults /Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/agent-config-studio-trunk/lib/roles.default.json, UI /Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/agent-config-studio-trunk/lib/roles-panel.js. Every skill resolves models through the model-id CLI (installed shim -> ACS code), so a change to how roles resolve reaches every skill at once.
+- No orchestrator role exists: the harness the user opens IS the orchestrator. A Claude Code session's main loop can only run Claude models (--model switches among Claude models; a gateway via ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL needs a paid OpenAI API key, not the ChatGPT/Codex plan). So "Sol orchestrates" realistically means opening the Codex CLI; Cris prefers the Claude Code UI.
+- ACS already has a Usage page reading per-account limits: /Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/agent-config-studio-trunk/lib/usage/ (claude.js, codex.js, codex-limits.js, grok.js, seats.js, accounts.js, percent.js); seats in ~/.agent-config-studio/seats.json and ~/.codex-seats/*. So remaining room per account is known.
+- Measured this session (Claude side only): builders 0.74M output tokens, orchestrator 0.31M output but ~182M input+cache (long conversation), docs writers small; reviews mostly ran on Codex (Sol) or separate headless Fable calls not counted.
+- Product direction (decided 2026-11-12): ACS = Cris's tool + portfolio + product; "if it confuses a new user it doesn't ship"; success = context, routing, checks, guardrails; routing is the differentiator; zero-config, every setting in a file the user owns; Cris's opinionated workflow is an optional pack, never a default. Build order approved: PR1 simplify (merged #88) -> Cris uses it a day -> PR2 report card (read-only mirror of the setup on those four parts, sketch first) -> PR3 Guardrails read-only -> PR4 writes.
+- Only real user today is Cris (69 npm downloads/month).
+
+## CURRENT DIRECTION (attack this)
+Add "profiles" to roles.json: Default = current roles untouched; named profiles (e.g. "Low Claude", "Low Codex") hold only overrides per role; one active profile; switch via a toggle on the Models page or "acs profile use <name>"; model-id resolves active profile over defaults so every skill follows. Add an advisory "orchestrator" role telling which harness to open. Later: Usage page suggests (never auto-switches) a profile when an account is near its limit. Ship it next, before the report card, as a small precise-lane PR (roles drive every review gate).
+
+## DECISIONS IN PLAY
+1. Shape for other users: hand-made named profiles, vs. a simpler "an account is low -> skip its families" rule (automatic fallback down each role's existing family list using known usage), vs. both. Which survives the confuse-a-new-user rule and works for single-plan users?
+2. Manual switch vs. suggested vs. automatic (usage-driven) switching, and where it shows (Models, Usage, report card).
+3. Orchestrator: is an "orchestrator role" meaningful when the harness decides, or just guidance text?
+4. Sequencing: before the report card, or as part of its Routing part.
+
+## READ FIRST
+- /Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/agent-config-studio-trunk/lib/roles.js
+- /Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/agent-config-studio-trunk/lib/roles.default.json
+- /Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/agent-config-studio-trunk/lib/roles-panel.js
+- /Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/agent-config-studio-trunk/lib/usage/accounts.js and /Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/agent-config-studio-trunk/lib/usage/percent.js
+- /Users/cortega/.claude/projects/-Users-cortega/memory/project-acs-product-direction.md
+- /Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/skills-work/builds/acs-reshape/decisions.md
diff --git a/builds/pause-account/advisor.out b/builds/pause-account/advisor.out
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..60cb141
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/pause-account/advisor.out
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+## 1. SCOPE VERDICT
+
+**Over-built** — the problem is real, but named profiles add a second copy of the roles system when a "pause this account" switch over the fallback lists Cris already has does the same job.
+
+## 2. ADVISORY
+
+I changed no repo or user files; the two tests ran against a throwaway home under `$TMPDIR`.
+
+**Build "pause", not profiles.** Store a user-owned list of paused families or vendors; `resolveRole` drops them from a role's ordered `use` list and answers with the next one.
+- **It already fits his setup.** Pausing Claude gives builder → sol, reviewer → sol/astra, security → astra; pausing Codex gives builder → opus, reviewer → fable/opus. No authoring needed.
+- **It reaches every skill.** `ask-model` (`tools/ask-model.mjs:732`) and the review pool (`packs/review-gate/runtime/review.mjs:515`) both go through `resolveRole`.
+- **It works for a single-plan user.** Claude limits are per model (`lib/usage/claude.js:94`), so "pause fable" falls to opus on the same plan.
+- **A new user understands it.** "Claude is low — pause it" needs no new concept; profiles need an editor, merge layers and names.
+
+**Keep the pause in its own file, not `roles.json`.**
+- **A new key breaks old resolvers.** I added `profiles` to a copy of his `roles.json`: every role returned `MODEL-ID-UNRESOLVED` (`lib/roles.js:117`). His installed resolver matches the shipped one today, but any other user who updates ACS without re-running `acs install-model-id` would lose every skill.
+- **It keeps the precise lane untouched.** No `writeRoles` change, no version 3, and "defaults untouched" is literally true.
+- **Reuse the existing guard.** Refuse to pause when `resolverStale` is true (`lib/roles-panel.js:64`), or an old resolver silently ignores the file.
+
+**What the pause version must include.**
+- **Loud output.** A stderr line and JSON fields naming what was skipped; the repo's rule is no silent fallback.
+- **Refusal when nothing is left.** Exit 2 with the fix, like an unset role. The writer role must refuse or stay exempt: it needs a Claude family in Claude Code (`packs/review-gate/skills/claude/context-pass/SKILL.md:42`).
+- **Named families still work.** `/build opus` or `REVIEW_REVIEWER=fable` should run while paused; pause affects role resolution only.
+- **One sentence in the model guide.** His `CLAUDE.md` block lists families per role; with profiles it would go stale on every switch and need a proposal-and-accept write per harness (`lib/model-guide.js:16-21`).
+- **A same-vendor notice.** With Claude paused, sol builds and sol/astra check it; say so in the UI.
+
+**Cut.**
+- **Named profiles, the profile editor and `acs profile`.** Add them only if he hits a routing that fallback order plus pause can't express.
+- **The orchestrator role.** A custom `orchestrator` role already resolves today with no code change (tested), no skill reads it, and the guide would print it into `CLAUDE.md`. Make it guidance text beside the switch.
+- **Automatic switching.** The saved snapshot was 46 hours old when I checked, and Codex readings stop counting after 60 minutes (`lib/usage/codex.js:158`). A suggestion is fine; put it in the report card's Routing part with "N roles have no fallback outside Claude".
+- **Multi-seat handling.** Two Codex seats is a `CODEX_HOME` choice, already covered by the shell shortcuts (`lib/usage/shell.js:162`). API keys have no plan limit to pause.
+
+**Set the expectation for "Low Claude".** The brief's own numbers put the main session at ~182M input+cache tokens against 0.74M builder output, and his builder is already sol-first. Pause moves only delegated Fable calls (review, judge, advisor, security), which were not counted. Measure that share in the first week; the larger lever is the main session (`claude --model opus`, or hand off and start fresh).
+
+**Put the switch on the Usage account row**, where the low account is seen, with Models → Roles showing the effect. `bin/usage.mjs:89` already prints "Route to:"; this gives that answer something to act on.
+
+## 3. QUESTIONS
+
+1. **Will you drop hand-made profiles for now in favour of pause?** Recommended: yes; revisit after two weeks if there is a routing you could not express.
+2. **When a paused role has no fallback left, refuse or promote its second opinion?** Recommended: refuse. Advisor, judge and investigator would refuse on day one, so add one fallback to each once; promoting would leave those roles with no second opinion.
+3. **Should a pause expire at the account's reset time?** Recommended: yes, prefilled from the reset time with an "until I resume" option; the realistic failure is forgetting to switch back.
+4. **Does this jump ahead of the report card?** Recommended: yes for the pause-sized version only; the suggestion and the "no fallback" finding go into the report card.
diff --git a/builds/pause-account/log.md b/builds/pause-account/log.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3518b8f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/pause-account/log.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Pause an account — build log
+
+## Phase 1: resolver + CLI
+- Pause reading lives in lib/roles.js (readPaused, pausedBy, pauseLine), so the existing resolverStale byte compare of the installed roles.js covers R6 with no new install file. vendorOf moved to lib/models.js (the resolver copies it); lib/models-catalog.js re-exports it.
+- resolveRole filters `use`/`ids`/`members` and `alt`; adds `paused`, `skipped` [{family, by}], `altSkipped` only while a pause is in force; `pauseError` when paused.json is invalid.
+- A name that is a vendor (grok) means the vendor, which already covers the family of that name.
+- ask-model keeps its usage exit (64) for a refused role, as it does for an unset one; model-id exits 2.
+- `acs pause <name>` with no flag ends at the vendor's tightest-window reset from the stored usage reading, else until resume (says so).
+- Resume is never refused for a stale resolver: an old resolver ignores pauses anyway.
+- Tests: tests/roles-pause.mjs (R1–R5, ask-model, reviewer pool via --show-config), tests/pause-cli.mjs (R1, R6, R9).
+
+## Phase 2: UI + routes
+- GET /api/pause, POST /api/pause {name, until|null}, POST /api/pause/resume {name}: strict same-origin. GET /api/models/roles carries `pause` (state + each role's answer, refusals, sameVendor).
+- Usage row: Pause (secondary) → "Until it resets (…)" (primary, only when the reading has a reset) / "Until I resume" / Cancel (quiet). Paused row: "Paused until …" + Resume. Family pauses show on their vendor's rows. Stale resolver or invalid file disables Pause with the reason.
+- Tests: tests/pause-routes.mjs (R6 server, R7, R8 data), tests/pause-ui.mjs (R7, R8, R11 styles).
+
+## Phase 3: docs
+- README "Pausing an account" under Subscription usage; acs help lists pause and resume.
+- R10's guide sentence landed in phase 1 with guideText; its test (and README's) are in tests/roles-pause.mjs.
diff --git a/builds/pause-account/plan.md b/builds/pause-account/plan.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f72f44c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/pause-account/plan.md
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# Pause an account — plan
+
+Decided with Cris 2026-11-13 after /advisor (Fable): build "pause", not named profiles. Answers: pause instead of profiles; a role left empty refuses; a pause ends at the account's reset by default ("until I resume" optional); ships before the report card. Advisor brief and answer: this folder.
+
+## Problem
+When one subscription runs low (e.g. Claude), every role that starts with that vendor's models keeps spending it. Changing roles to work around it means editing defaults and remembering to change them back. Other users have the same problem with other mixes of plans.
+
+## Outcome (one PR: the resolver change and its switch only work together)
+- R1 **Pause file.** `~/.agent-config-studio/paused.json` (user-owned, separate from roles.json): a list of paused vendors (claude, codex, grok) and/or families, each with an optional `until` time. Missing file = nothing paused. roles.json is never written by this feature.
+- R2 **Resolution.** `resolveRole` skips paused families (and families of a paused vendor) in a role's ordered `use` list and answers with the next one; the second opinion (`alt`) is skipped the same way, becoming empty. Expired entries are ignored. Every path that already uses resolveRole follows: model-id, ask-model, the review pool, /build, /advisor.
+- R3 **Loud.** When something is skipped, model-id prints one stderr line ("claude paused: reviewer → sol (skipped fable)"), and its JSON carries `paused` and `skipped` fields. No silent fallback.
+- R4 **Refuse when empty.** A role whose every family is paused exits 2 with a plain fix ("every model for advisor is paused; resume claude or add a fallback in ACS → Models → Roles"). The writer role is not exempt: it refuses the same way.
+- R5 **Names still work.** A family named directly (`model-id opus`, `/build opus`, `REVIEW_REVIEWER=fable`, `ask-model --family`) is not affected by a pause.
+- R6 **Stale resolver guard.** Pausing from ACS is refused while the installed model-id is older than the one that reads paused.json (existing `resolverStale`), with the existing "re-run acs install-model-id" fix; an old resolver must never silently ignore a pause.
+- R7 **The switch, on Usage.** Each account row gets Pause / Resume. Pausing offers "until <reset time>" (pre-filled from the reading, when known) or "until I resume". A paused account shows "Paused until …".
+- R8 **Effect, on Models → Roles.** While anything is paused, a notice lists each role's current answer and marks roles that would refuse, and a same-vendor note when builder and reviewer now come from one vendor.
+- R9 **CLI.** `acs pause <vendor|family> [--until <time>|--until-resume]`, `acs resume <vendor|family>`, `acs pause` (lists).
+- R10 **Model guide.** One sentence in the generated guide block: roles skip paused accounts; `model-id --role <r>` gives the current answer. No per-switch rewrite of instruction files.
+- R11 **UI rules.** Styled buttons, no folds, ≥12px, plain words, light and dark; README documents pause.
+
+## Out of scope
+Named profiles; an orchestrator role; automatic switching or usage-driven suggestions (report card later); multi-seat logic; changing anyone's roles; the review gate itself beyond reading resolveRole.
+
+## Acceptance
+- Unit tests: skip by vendor and by family; alt skipped; expired pause ignored; empty role refuses with exit 2 and the fix; named family unaffected; missing/invalid paused.json = nothing paused (invalid reported, never crashes).
+- model-id stderr line and JSON fields; ask-model and review pool pick the next family under pause (test with a temp HOME).
+- Route + UI tests for Pause/Resume on Usage, notice on Roles, CLI commands; resolverStale refusal.
+- Existing suites pass; changed assertions only in test-only commits.
+- One browser QA at the end on a sandbox studio.
+
+Lane: precise (roles drive every review gate). One PR. Builder: Opus (xhigh; resolver logic).
+After merge: Cris adds one fallback each to advisor, judge and investigator in ACS (his setting), so a Claude pause doesn't empty them.
