packs/build/skills/claude/build/SKILL.md:43:**The session model orchestrates and guides. A builder types. A different brain verifies. The human judges.** Whatever model runs this session is the orchestrator, and it does NOT type the bulk of the code. Families come from the ACS roles (`model-id --role <role>`); your own instruction file may add rules the roles can't express. Whoever implements never grades their own work.
packs/build/skills/claude/build/SKILL.md:83:5. **Codex-lane steering uses session resume, not re-invocation.** Capture the `thread_id` from the first phase's `--json` output and keep it for the whole build. Every callback answer and every subsequent phase goes through `codex exec resume <thread_id>` — codex continues with its full context intact, so a one-line answer stays a one-line answer instead of a rebuilt brief. Only start a fresh session if you are deliberately resetting a poisoned context.
