packs/build/skills/claude/build/SKILL.md:139:**Build — phase 1 on a codex-CLI builder (the only call that starts a session).** `--json` so you can capture the `thread_id`; `-o` so the checkpoint lands in a file instead of buried in event noise. This is the ONLY codex call that gets `--sandbox workspace-write`:
packs/build/skills/claude/build/SKILL.md:142:  --json -o builds/<slug>/phase1-result.md \
packs/build/skills/claude/build/SKILL.md:160:`resume` does NOT accept `-s/--sandbox` — it inherits the sandbox policy from the session it resumes, which is why phase 1 must be the one that sets `workspace-write`. It does accept `-m`, `-c`, `-o`, `--json`, `--skip-git-repo-check`. Prefer an explicit `thread_id` over `--last`: the Bounce and Grade gates run in the same cwd, so `--last` can silently resume the wrong session. On a claude-CLI builder the phases go to a subagent on that family at the run's effort instead of these codex calls; the gates stay on their roles regardless of lane.
